om/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T13:54:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T13:54:47Z","body":"Do it in whatever way is the easiest to review. Too few changes per PR creates overhead, but too many at once makes it hard to give each change the necessary attention.\r\n\r\nIn this case maybe use one PR for effects, one for ogg and mp3 (and playbacks), and one for the rest. But you decide what fits thematically :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3891102331/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3903691531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116199#issuecomment-3903691531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116199","id":3903691531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7orZsL","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-15T08:11:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T08:11:05Z","body":"This is open and ready for review now. Would be good to get reviews from people knowledgeable of audio too!\r\n\r\nI was thinking of including additional material, like how `AudioEffectSpectrumAnalyzer` has one for FFT. Do you think some could be included? Which classes? I was thinking of Capture and Compressor. They can be a bit hard to grasp, I think.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3903691531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3918157056","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116199#issuecomment-3918157056","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116199","id":3918157056,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pilUA","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T02:32:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T02:35:34Z","body":"Pushed a new commit, to see new diffs clearly. Let me know when it's all okay, so I can squash. I apologize for how big this docs PR is. I didn't think it'd take this much work, but I think this is the best way I could've approached it.\r\nI tried to follow all suggestions, as well as keeping some consistency and improving flow here and there. My goal with this commit was to reduce some audio jargon and make it more friendly to people unfamiliar with the topic, and describe things with game devs in mind, not people specifically working with audio\r\nIf I missed some things, or think some changes should be reverted, please let me know. I'd love to see this merged :)\r\n\r\nEdit: still unsure if new filters can be made from `AudioEffectFilter`, so I didn't comment on that the same way it's written in `AudioEffectEQ`. I also didn't add any additional material, even though some classes could probably use it. I might consider adding if I have to work on this more. Otherwise, I'll make it a separate PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3918157056/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues